messages:
maya: Heads-up — I'm planning to swap the inference-cache Deployment -> StatefulSet to stabilize PV attachment and make scale-down safer. Will submit a Terraform change + k8s manifest tweak. Plan: canary (partition=1), increase replicas 3->5, reduce sidecar cpu requests. Any blockers?

kevin: Can you drop the PR link? also what's the secret rotation plan and PV reclaim policy? If sticky storage isn't required i'd prefer staying as a Deployment.

maya: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/789 — main change in modules/k8s/sts.tf. Secrets: we'll swap the k8s secret and annotate pods to force rolling restart; KMS key id will be rotated in the secret. PVC reclaimPolicy remains Retain for now. Example terraform snippet I pasted in the PR:

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "inference_cache" {
  metadata { name = "inference-cache" }
  spec {
    service_name = "inference-cache-headless"
    replicas = 3
    template {
      spec {
        containers {
          name = "cache"
          resources { requests = { cpu = "200m" memory = "256Mi" } }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

sarah: Heads-up — readiness probes are critical here. With stateful set + init containers you can end up stuck if initialDelay is too short. Recommend readiness.initialDelaySeconds: 30 and failureThreshold: 5. For canary use partition = replicas - 1 so only one pod updates first. Also consider podAntiAffinity to avoid noisy-neighbor effects.

kevin: :thumbsup: Add a canary label (canary=true) and disable HPA during the canary window. Watch PVC sizes and reclaimPolicy as maya said.

engbot: terraform-plan-bot: ran plan on branch maya/sts-swap — no plan drift, 2 resources to be replaced, 1 secret to be updated. Plan link: http://ci.internal/plan/2243

maya: Thanks. I'll hold the rollout until PM signs off. I'm going to set strategy to keep latency stable: maxUnavailable=0, maxSurge=1 and partition=1 for the initial canary. Quick YAML snippet for the strategy I put in the PR: 

```yaml
strategy:
  type: RollingUpdate
  rollingUpdate:
    maxUnavailable: 0
    maxSurge: 1
    partition: 1
```

ethan: If we move to a StatefulSet remember to use a headless service so we keep stable network identities. svc should be ClusterIP: None and selector matching pod labels. I'll add that to the PR.

sarah: Ping me when PR is ready for review @sarah — I'll run through the canary checklist and latency smoke tests (tail p99 for 15m, run a few synthetic queries).

maya: PTAL: PR updated with headless svc, readiness tweak, and reduced sidecar cpu. Will run canary tonight at 22:00 UTC. cc @kevin @ethan

kevin: ACK — if smoke passes i'll approve and trigger apply. :rocket:

deploy-bot: apply-job: started apply for branch maya/sts-swap — performing 1-pod canary (partition=1) then will continue. Monitor logs: https://logs.internal/redwood/12345

maya: Noted, i'll monitor logs and post canary metrics here after the run.
